Subject: [PATCH] feat(db): add additive marketplace_events log (Provider
 Activation Phase 1)

Phase 1 (schema/migration only) of the Provider Activation & First Booking
Conversion checkpoint. Adds a generic, append-only marketplace_events table for
activation + client-conversion funnel measurement, plus stable typed enums
(marketplace_event_type, marketplace_event_reason_code, marketplace_event_source).

Envelope: event_type, occurred_at/recorded_at, actor_user_id/actor_role,
provider_profile_id (business/tenant key), client_user_id, service_id, booking_id,
correlation_id, source, metadata (jsonb; IDs/typed values only, no PII/secrets),
reason_code. Foreign keys use ON DELETE SET NULL (erasure-friendly). Indexes for
type/provider/client funnels, correlation stitching, and time-range reporting.

Strictly additive: applied via drizzle-kit push; exactly 1 table + 3 enums created,
zero existing objects altered or dropped. No readiness logic, event emission,
booking enforcement, discovery gating, reporting API, or UI in this phase.
Rollback: DROP TABLE marketplace_events, then DROP the 3 dependent enum types.

Validation: typecheck green; existing API suites green (reviewer-decisions 14/14,
provider-notifications 12/12, provider-application 8/8, provider-status 9/9).
